/**************************************************************************
 *
 * PROJECT:	Icon Editor	(GOC Version)
 * FILE:	iconed.goh
 *
 *		This project is inspired by the Icon Editor by Steve Yegge, 1992 - 1994
 *
 * REVISION HISTORY:
 *	Name	Date		Description
 *	----	----		-----------
 *	RainerB 7/18/2025	Initial version
 *	RainerB 10/17/2025	Pre-Release 0.99
 *
 *
 * TERMS:
 *
 * One of the problems for the Icon Editor is that there is no exact definition of
 * what an icon actually is. In the SDK, the term is used both for a set of images
 * from which GEOS selects the appropriate one depending on the situation, and for
 * the individual images themselves.
 *
 * In the community, the term icon is mainly used for the individual images. There
 * is no specific term for a set of icons.
 *
 * Note: If you know the old version of the Icon Editor, you may remember that the
 * 	term icon was used exclusively for a set of images and the term format was
 *	used for the individual images and their properties.
 *	In discussions with the community, it became clear that the term format is
 *	not appropriate here; moreover, many users find it confusing.
 *
 * Therefore, I use the term 'icon' for the individual images. The collection of
 * icons, from which GEOS selects the appropriate one depending on the situation,
 * is called an 'icon set'.
 *
 * In a perfect world, this terminology would be reflected 1:1 in the code. In our
 * case, however, the terms 'icon' and 'icon set' are very similar. Therefore,
 * for data structures or objects that explicitly refer to a single icon from the
 * set, often the term IconEntry is used if the term icon could be ambiguous.
 *
 * Hence, the following terms are used:
 *
 *	database	This is the document file of the program.
 *			It contains one or more icon sets.
 *	icon set	An icon set is a collection of (small) images
 *			An icon set can be exported to the TokenDatabase file, for example
 *			This program usually refers a icon set using the ISetHeader
 *			structure, defined in iconFile.goh.
 *	icon		This usually means one of the images (and its properties)
 * 			of an particular icon set, usually referred by an IconEntry
 * 			structure, which is defined in iconFile.goh.
 *
 *	ISetHeader	A structure that describes an icon set
 *	IconEntry	A structure that describes a particular icon from a set
 *
 *	mainArray	A HugeArray of ISetHeader structures.
 *	iEntryList	A ChunkArray of IconEntry structures.
 *
 *	token		A token consists of 4 letters and a word. It can be
 *			interpreted as an index in the token database file and
 *			references an 'icon set' in this file.
 *
 *
 **************************************************************************/

#ifndef _ICONED_GOH
#define _ICONED_GOH

